      <div type="clause" n="30.6">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 30.6</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30.6" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="334" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he þonne ut hleape<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_30-6.lnote.oe.7-2"/> ⁊ þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ordal forbuge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_30-6.lnote.oe.8-2"/>, gilde se borh ðam teonde his ceapgyld<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_30-6.lnote.oe.9-2"/> ⁊ þam cingce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_30-6.lnote.oe.10"/> his wer oððe þam þe his wites wurðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_30-6.lnote.oe.11"/> sig.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30.6" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="334" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf he ðonne ut leape ⁊ þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ordal forbuge, gylde se borh ðam teonde his ceapgyld ⁊ ðam cynge his wer oððe ðam ðe his weres wyrðe sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30.6" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="334" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he þonne ut leape ⁊ þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ordal forbugan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_30-6.lnote.oe.1"/>, gylde se borh þam teonde his ceapgild ⁊ þam cyninge his wer oððe þam þe his wites wurðe sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="30.6" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="335" ed="#liebermann"/>Si aufugerit et ordalium uitauerit, soluat plegius compellanti (repetenti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_30-6.lnote.oe.4-2"/>) captale suum et regi wéram suam uel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_30-6.lnote.oe.5-2"/> ei qui<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_30-6.lnote.oe.6-2"/> wíta sua dignus erit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="30.6" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="335" ed="#liebermann"/>Quodsi calumniatus euaserit et iudicium declinauerit, fideiussores reddant calumnianti quod á latrone exegit, et regi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_30-6.lnote.oe.2"/> prętium latronis aut illi qui habet sacę<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_30-6.lnote.oe.3-2"/> et socne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="30.6" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="335" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui si sub fideiussione effugerit et Dei iudicium sic deuitauerit, soluat fideiussor calumpniatori capitalem censum et regi redempcionem eius uel illi qui forisfactura illius dignus sit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="30.6" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="190" ed="#robertson"/>Gyf he ðonne ut leape ⁊ þæt ordal forbuge, gylde se borh ðam teonde his ceapgyld ⁊ ðam cynge his wer oððe ðam ðe his weres<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#IICn_30-6.robnote.fn.13"/> wyrðe sy.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="272" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Gif he þonne ut hleape and þæt ordal forbuge, gilde se borh ðam teonde his ceapgyld and þam cingce his wer oððe þam þe his wites wurðe sig.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="334" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn [Verklagt]er aber entflieht und das Ordal vermeidet, so zahle der Bürge dem Kläger dessen Schadenersatz, und des [Verklagten] Wergeld dem König<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_30-6.lnote.de.1"/> oder dem, der berechtigt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_30-6.lnote.de.2"/> ist zum [durch Verklagten zu verwirkenden] Strafgeld (Wergeld <hi rend="italic">B</hi>).</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">But if [the accused] escapes and avoids the ordeal, let the surety pay the plaintiff his compensation for the goods, and [the accused's] wergild to the king or to the one who is entitled to the fine (wergild, B) [forfeited by the accused].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_30-6.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="191" ed="#robertson"/>If, however, he escapes and avoids the ordeal, his surety shall pay the value of his goods to the plaintiff and the wergeld of the accused to the king or to the man who is entitled to receive his wergeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="466" ed="#whitelock"/>If, however, he runs away and avoids the ordeal, the surety is to pay to the accuser the value of his property, and his wergild to the king or to the man who is entitled to his fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="273" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Yet if he escapes and shuns the ordeal, his surety is to give the market value of his goods to the accuser and the value of his wergild to the king or to whoever is entitled to receive that fine.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="334"><ref target="clause:IAtr_1-7">I Atr 1.7</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. I Atr. 1, 7</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="321"><label>differs; Cnut remedied</label> <ref target="clause:IAtr_1-7">I Atr 1.7</ref> <quote>there is also a difference between I Atr 1:7 and II Cn 30:6 ... it is not inconceivable that I Atr had these (very minor) defects from the outset, and that Cnut remedied them</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:IAtr_1-7">I Atr 1.7</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 30:6: I Atr 1:7</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="206"><label>derives from</label> <ref target="clause:IAtr_1-7">I Atr 1.7</ref> <quote>4 l. II Cnut 30:3b,6 (I Æthelred 1:5,7, except where in bold)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="207"><ref target="clause:IIAs_1-5">II As 1.5</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">A's ‘forbugan’ is a Middle English verb form. Liebermann compares I Atr 1.7.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 335, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">wites: weres B</note>
